+---
+id: PLAN-012-sessions-search
+status: draft
+date: 2026-11-05
+review_count: 0
+patch: n/a
+---
+
+# PLAN-012: Search/filter box on the Sessions page
+
+## Status
+
+draft
+
+## Context
+
+The Sessions page (`web/src/pages/Sessions.tsx`) renders every stored
+session in a table. As the session count grows, finding a past session
+means eyeballing the list. The user asked for a text input at the top of
+the list that filters sessions as they type: case-insensitive match
+against the session title/name and date, a clear empty-state message
+when nothing matches, and the full list restored when the input is
+cleared. No submit button, same visual style as the rest of the page.
+
+## Governing records
+
+- BDR-001: personal single-user tool; the full session list is already
+  fetched client-side, so filtering is client-side only - no server
+  search endpoint, no pagination concerns at this scale.
+- BDR-002: zero new dependencies, zero added cost; the shadcn `Input`
+  component is already vendored in `web/src/components/ui/input.tsx`.
+- ADR-001: SPA on localhost; this change is a frontend-internal concern,
+  the REST surface is untouched.
+- ADR-006: React + TypeScript + Tailwind + shadcn/ui; the shadcn policy
+  is satisfied because no new component is needed (`input.tsx` exists).
+  Vitest runs `*.test.ts` files in `environment: 'node'`, so the
+  filterable logic must live in a pure function under `web/src/lib/`
+  rather than inside the component. `tsc --noEmit` is the typecheck gate.
+- ADR-007: the read path is `listSessions` returning `SessionSummary`;
+  filtering operates on that shape. `SessionSummary` has no `title`
+  field - the session's name as displayed is `s.id` (`<slug>-<HHmm>`,
+  rendered in the "Session" column) and its date is `s.started_at`
+  rendered via `toLocaleString()`.
+
+## Scope
+
+In scope:
+
+1. A pure `filterSessions` helper in `web/src/lib/session-filter.ts`
+   plus its unit test.
+2. `Sessions.tsx`: a controlled search `Input` inside the card, above
+   the table, filtering as the user types; a no-match empty state that
+   keeps the input visible.
+
+Out of scope: server-side search or new API parameters, matching
+transcript content/speaker names/duration/provider, debouncing (the
+list is already in memory; filtering is synchronous and trivial),
+sorting, persisting the query in the URL, and any change to the
+"no sessions yet" page-level empty state.
+
+## Contracts (literal)
+
+**Filter function** (`web/src/lib/session-filter.ts`):
+
+```ts
+import type { SessionSummary } from './types';
+
+export function filterSessions(
+  sessions: SessionSummary[],
+  query: string,
+): SessionSummary[];
+```
+
+Semantics, pinned:
+
+- `const q = query.trim().toLowerCase()`; when `q === ''`, return the
+  input array unchanged (restores the full list on clear).
+- Otherwise a session is kept when `q` is a substring of its haystack,
+  the lowercased concatenation of:
+  - `s.id` (the session name shown in the first column),
+  - `s.started_at ?? ''` (raw ISO timestamp, so `2026-11-04` matches),
+  - `s.started_at` formatted with `new Date(...).toLocaleString()` when
+    `started_at` is non-null and parses to a valid date
+    (`Number.isNaN(d.getTime())` guards; invalid/missing dates
+    contribute nothing), so typing the date as displayed matches.
+- Pure function: no mutation, order preserved, no side effects.
+
+**User-facing strings** (verbatim):
+
+- Input attributes: `type="search"`, `placeholder="Search sessions…"`,
+  `aria-label="Search sessions"`, `className="mb-3 max-w-sm"`.
+- No-match empty state: `EmptyTitle` = `No matching sessions`;
+  `EmptyDescription` = `No sessions match "<query>". Try a different
+  name or date.` (literal quotes around the trimmed query).
+
+## Steps
+
+### Step 1 - `web/src/lib/session-filter.ts` + `.test.ts`
+
+- New file exporting `filterSessions` per the pinned contract.
+- New file `session-filter.test.ts` next to it (see Test plan).
+
+### Step 2 - `web/src/pages/Sessions.tsx`: wire the input
+
+- Add `const [query, setQuery] = useState('')` next to the existing
+  `sessions`/`activeId` state.
+- After the loading and `sessions.length === 0` early returns (both
+  unchanged), compute `const visible = filterSessions(sessions, query)`
+  inline per render; no `useMemo` at this list size.
+- Inside `CardContent`, above the `Table`, render the `Input` with the
+  pinned attributes; `onChange` calls `setQuery(e.target.value)`.
+- When `visible.length === 0`, render the existing `Empty` family
+  (`EmptyHeader` > `EmptyMedia variant="icon"` with the lucide
+  `SearchX` icon, `EmptyTitle`, `EmptyDescription` per the pinned copy)
+  in place of the `Table`, keeping the input visible above it.
+- Otherwise render the existing `Table` over `visible` unchanged,
+  including the `activeId` live badge and the Live/Review buttons.
+- New imports only: `useState` already imported; add `Input` from
+  `@/components/ui/input`, `SearchX` from `lucide-react`, and
+  `filterSessions` from `@/lib/session-filter`.
+- Edge cases: the live-session row filters like any other row; a query
+  that is only whitespace behaves as empty; `started_at: null` rows
+  still match on `id`. No failure/cleanup semantics: no fetch, no
+  effect, no timers.
+
+## Test plan
+
+Automated (`web/src/lib/session-filter.test.ts`, vitest, node env -
+matches the existing lib-test convention):
+
+- Empty query and whitespace-only query return the full list.
+- Case-insensitive substring match on `id` (e.g. query `STANDUP`
+  matches id `standup-1430`).
+- Substring match on the raw ISO `started_at` (e.g. `2026-11-04`).
+- Match on the displayed date: the test derives
+  `new Date(started_at).toLocaleString()` itself and queries a slice of
+  it, so the assertion is locale-independent.
+- Non-matching query returns `[]`.
+- `started_at: null` sessions do not throw and still match on `id`.
+
+Gates (task requirement): `npm test` and `npm run typecheck` must pass.
+Per repo convention also run `npm --prefix web run lint` and
+`npm --prefix web run build`.
+
+Manual acceptance (browser):
+
+- Typing in the box narrows the table on each keystroke; no submit.
+- A query matching no session shows the empty-state message; editing
+  or clearing the query restores matching rows, clearing fully
+  restores the whole list.
+- Input looks consistent with the page (same shadcn styling).
+
+## Risks and notes
+
+- Assumption: "session title/name" means `s.id` - `SessionSummary` has
+  no separate title field; the `id` (slug + time) is the only name the
+  UI displays. If a friendly title is added later, extend the haystack.
+- Assumption: "date" means `started_at` as shown in the Started column;
+  matching the raw ISO string is added so `YYYY-MM-DD` queries work
+  even under non-ISO locales.
+- `toLocaleString()` output varies by user locale; that is correct
+  behavior (match what the user sees) and is why the unit test derives
+  its needle from the same call rather than a hardcoded string.
+- No React component-test infrastructure exists in the repo (vitest is
+  `environment: 'node'`; no testing-library/jsdom), so the page wiring
+  is covered by manual acceptance, consistent with previous UI plans.
+- `type="search"` gives a native clear affordance in WebKit browsers;
+  clearing by deleting the text works identically.
+- `Empty` without `className="mt-20 border"` is intentional inside the
+  card: the bordered offset variant stays reserved for the page-level
+  "no sessions yet" state.
+- Follow-up outside this plan: if session volume grows enough to need
+  content search, ADR-007 already designates a SQLite index as the next
+  step.
+
+## Definition of Done
+
+- [ ] `filterSessions` in `web/src/lib/session-filter.ts` implements the
+  pinned contract (trim, lowercase, substring, haystack = id + ISO +
+  locale string, empty query returns full list).
+- [ ] `Sessions.tsx` renders the pinned `Input` above the table inside
+  the card, filters `visible` rows as the user types with no submit,
+  and shows the pinned `Empty` block on zero matches while the input
+  stays visible.
+- [ ] `session-filter.test.ts` covers the listed cases; `npm test` and
+  `npm run typecheck` pass (plus `npm --prefix web run lint` and
+  `npm --prefix web run build` clean).
+- [ ] Manual acceptance list verified in the browser.
-- 
